       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily is 9,000 mg/day, which is more than double the usual maximum of 4,000 mg/day for adults. Even 4,000 mg/day is often capped at 3,000 mg/day in practice. A single 3,000 mg dose is also three times the usual 1,000 mg maximum. This regimen carries a serious risk of acute liver injury and liver failure, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg PO four times daily** (4,000 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day)\n- **3000 mg total per day**, divided into smaller doses\n\nIf you do want the 3000 mg three-times-daily regimen as written, tell me the clinical rationale. I would still suggest a pharmacy review before it's entered.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose and frequency, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
