       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 9,000 mg/day has no therapeutic use, and the risk of hepatotoxicity is high enough that I can't treat it as a routine order. A single 3,000 mg dose is itself in the range where toxicity is a concern. Normal liver function and a weight of 70 kg don't make it safe.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **Change the dose.** I can enter 1000 mg PO three or four times daily (3,000\u20134,000 mg/day) right away.\n- **Consult pharmacy or toxicology.** If the order is meant for something unusual, they can review it and help enter it through the proper channels.\n- **Enter it yourself.** If you still believe this is correct, you can place it directly with the pharmacist's verification. I won't submit it from here.\n\nDo you want me to enter one of the standard regimens?"
      }
